CowSwapModule_Execute
├── when amount is zero
│   ├── it should return failed result with zero sell amount reason
│   └── it should not create an order or lock tokens
├── when target token is zero address
│   └── it should return failed result with zero target token reason
├── when target token equals sell token
│   └── it should return failed result with same sell and buy token reason
├── when min buy amount is zero
│   └── it should return failed result with zero minimum buy amount reason
├── when validity duration is zero
│   └── it should return failed result with zero validity duration reason
├── when validity duration overflows uint32
│   ├── it should return failed result with validity duration overflow reason
│   └── it should not lock any tokens
├── when order id collides with existing order
│   ├── it should return failed result with order id collision reason
│   ├── it should not overwrite existing order metadata
│   └── it should not lock a second set of tokens
├── when a different app data produces a different order id
│   ├── it should succeed
│   └── it should create two independent orders with distinct order ids
├── when paymentRails has insufficient sell token balance
│   └── it should return failed result with insufficient balance reason
├── when token transfer fails (returns false)
│   ├── it should return failed result with token transfer failed reason
│   ├── it should clean up order metadata (CEI rollback — no stale collision)
│   ├── it should zero all struct fields in _orders mapping
│   └── it should cause isValidSignature to return FAILURE for the cleaned-up orderId
├── when token transfer reverts
│   └── it should clean up order metadata (CEI rollback — no stale collision)
├── when sell token reenters execute during transferFrom
│   └── it should revert the reentrant call (ReentrancyGuard)
├── when sell token reenters cancelOrder during execute transferFrom
│   └── it should revert the reentrant cancelOrder (shared ReentrancyGuard lock)
├── when no-return sell token (e.g. USDT)
│   └── it should succeed and store order metadata
├── when concurrent orders share the same sell token
│   ├── it should use accumulated approval after second order
│   ├── it should preserve second order approval after first order is mark filled
│   └── it should preserve second order approval after first order is cancelled
└── when all parameters are valid
    ├── it should transfer sell token from paymentRails to module
    ├── it should approve cow settlement for sell amount
    ├── it should store order metadata with pending status
    ├── it should store correct paymentRails address in metadata
    ├── it should store correct sell token in metadata
    ├── it should store correct buy token in metadata
    ├── it should store correct sell amount in metadata
    ├── it should store correct min buy amount in metadata
    ├── it should emit OrderCreated event
    ├── it should return success equals true
    ├── it should return amountOut equals zero
    ├── it should return outputToken equals buy token
    └── it should return data as encoded order id
